Let the standalone generator emit BF16 GEMMs that round C back to BF16.

The CLI only accepted F32 C for BF16 inputs, so add a BF16_VNNI_A precision
(A, B and C in BF16, F32 compute, A pre-packed in K pairs) and give the
inline-assembly emitter a C signature for it. On SPR the AMX kernel then moves
C between memory and its F32 tiles through the GEMM scratch on the stack:
vmovdqu16 + vpmovsxwd + vpslld widen each column of C to F32 into the scratch
for tileloadd, and tilestored to the scratch + vcvtne(2)ps2bf16 round the
accumulators back. Fix the text emitter for that path, which until now only
the JIT encoder had exercised:

- the stores and loads of the stack variables (alu_mem), among them the GEMM
  scratch pointer, printed nothing, so the kernel addressed the scratch
  through an uninitialised register; print the movq;
- vpmovsxwd had no mnemonic, so an uninitialised buffer was printed in its
  place;
- the two-operand forms of vec_compute (vpmovsxwd, vpslld $imm,
  vcvtneps2bf16) printed the undefined second source as %zmm255; they now
  print two operands, with the half-width source of vpmovsxwd and the
  half-width destination of vcvtneps2bf16.

The kernels the datasets measure -- SP and DP on skx and clx, BF16 with F32 C
on cpx -- are byte-identical. Elsewhere the now printed stores of stack
variables appear (the AMX kernels with F32 C store the scratch pointer they
never read back), and two-operand forms that did not assemble are repaired.

